  "editorial": {
    "title": "Apache HTTP/2 flaw makes exposure checks and patching urgent",
    "summary": "Apache identifies CVE-2026-119618 in mod_http2, affecting HTTP Server 2.4.55 through 2.4.70. The fix shipped in 2.4.71 on November 11. This is a disclosed RCE vulnerability; Aikido reported no known in-the-wild exploitation as of November 13.",
    "why_it_matters": "HTTP/2 configuration and the protocol reaching the backend determine exposure. A version match or a vendor’s cloud prevalence percentage does not establish an exploitable deployment.",
    "action": "Apply Apache 2.4.71 or a vendor-confirmed backport. If patching must wait, review disabling HTTP/2 and verify that the backend no longer accepts it.",
